# Issue: #48
**Issue**: #48
Feature: Fill shifts with clear mobile-first journeys
  Existing authoritative workflow, local time, security, privacy, and previews remain unchanged.

  Scenario: Volunteer scans an open primary or backup slot on a narrow phone
    Given a published opening has a group-local date, slot, location and signup policy
    When the volunteer visits Open shifts at 320 CSS pixels
    Then the title, local start, slot, text availability and claim or request outcome precede one primary action
    And full commitment details and recurring service remain accessible without JavaScript
    And the document does not scroll horizontally

  Scenario: Volunteer requests an approval-required slot
    Given the opening requires coordinator approval
    When the volunteer opens its request form and submits valid contact details
    Then the form explains that a coordinator reviews the request and shows the privacy notice
    And the private hub presents pending status and only actions valid for current authoritative state

  Scenario: Volunteer directly claims a slot
    Given the opening uses Direct claim
    When the volunteer opens its form
    Then the primary action says Claim commitment and the policy explains immediate confirmation for an eligible volunteer
    And the same backend first-eligible-wins and current status rules apply

  Scenario: Volunteer recovers a lost private commitment link
    Given a volunteer no longer has their private status link
    When they return to Open shifts
    Then a visible secondary link leads to the existing recovery form
    And its response does not disclose whether a commitment matched

  Scenario: Recurring service is reviewed before submission
    Given a volunteer chooses a recurring role, first date and horizon
    When they preview the exact included and unavailable dates
    Then review is the only pre-preview submit action
    And after preview the claim or request submit becomes primary beneath the exact dates
    And on the private recurring hub a valid confirm or withdrawal action precedes the long occurrence list

  Scenario: Coordinator navigates a compact header without script
    Given an allowlisted coordinator views the application at 320 CSS pixels with JavaScript disabled
    When they tab through Home, Work, Schedule and activate More coordinator pages with Enter or Space
    Then every existing secondary route and the sign-out POST remains focusable and operable
    And the header does not push the page title behind eleven stacked primary links

  Scenario: Coordinator resolves the most urgent coverage work
    Given the authoritative prioritized queue includes an uncovered slot or a pending approval
    When the coordinator follows Home to Work and opens the first intervention
    Then queue work appears before optional filters and the action names its intervention
    And Coverage foregrounds Assign volunteer for an open slot or Requests foregrounds Approve and assign for an eligible pending request
    And replacement, cancellation, decline, access, and filter paths remain accessible
    And server-rendered confirmation previews and audited transitions remain intact

  Scenario: Coordinator follows existing preview and confirm controls
    Given a coordinator has set the group time zone and entered a valid recurring pattern
    When they choose Preview dates or Save recurring schedule
    Then the corresponding existing server handler shows concrete dates or saves the schedule
    And a reviewed publication, revision or handoff confirmation reaches its existing handler rather than silently redisplaying the form

  Scenario: An eligible policy correction keeps its reviewed consequence
    Given a coordinator edits a shift and changes its signup policy
    When they preview the consequence and confirm the change
    Then the existing save action accepts the same reviewed consequence checked by the authoritative command
    And stale or ineligible changes remain blocked

  Scenario: Hub presents valid actions without a new capability
    Given a volunteer has a valid private status capability
    When the assignment state changes
    Then textual request and assignment states precede currently offered actions
    And no added interface bypasses token expiration, single-use semantics, eligibility deadlines or privacy controls
